  The reel_script says the onion price was 'கிலோ 200 ரூபாய் வரை' at the market, but the article says Rs.200 is the retail price and Rs.180 the wholesale price; the reel_script and slides_spec headline present Rs.200 as the market price without stating the wholesale/retail distinction clearly.
  The slides_spec title 'இன்றைய விலை' and the phrase 'இந்த விலை' in the first slide imply a single current price of Rs.180 at the market, mixing the wholesale figure with the article's 'கடந்த 3 ஆண்டுகளுக்குப் பிறகு' claim, which the article attaches to the retail-level Rs.200 price in the headline sense.
  The caption's 'நாள்: 20 நவம்பர் 2026' line is part of the footer and not a claim, but the caption text 'விலை கிடுகிடுவென உயர்ந்து வருகிறது' is accurate; no further issue there.
  The reel_script omits the article's note that prices rose from Rs.120-140 at the start of last month to Rs.160 before Deepavali, which is present, so no omission; however the reel_script states 'கடந்த மூன்று ஆண்டுகளில் இல்லாத அளவுக்கு' which is a slight mismatch with the article's wording 'கடந்த மூன்று ஆண்டுகளுக்கு பிறகு' (after three years), meaning the same price had not been seen in three years, not that it is the highest in three years.
